      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEAL TITAN NZ (7) kicked off his career in good style two-and-a-half weeks ago, beaten 5 metres into third over 2185m at Pinjarra. Drawn to enjoy an economical run and might sweat on the sprint lane. This is a nice drop in class and is set to continue his bright start to racing. DEFEND THE RIGHT (2) finished third at his most recent outing, beaten 3 metres, in a nice return to form at Pinjarra over 1684m. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Has the ability to take care of this field. THE SEA SIREN (9) is next in line and although she has to contend with an awkward gate a win is not out of the question. LIANAKA (4) was out of the money two runs ago then broke after suffering interference and finished fourth last start over 2190m at this track, arriving 5 metres behind the winner. Only needs to get things right to be in the money.",
